■ INTUITUM
PROJECT: 𝑒

///

CONTACT: SUPPORT@INTUITUM.SH
LOCATION: USA
STATUS: DEVELOPMENT

///

OVERVIEW:
 - Small, fast coding agent for the terminal.
 - One Rust binary with tools, commands, themes, prompts, and skills.
 - Executable JSONL extensions add tools, commands, hooks, side panes, and startup behavior.
 - Packages share extensions, skills, prompts, and themes: e install npm:<name>, or git:<host>/<user>/<repo>

///

INSTALL:
 curl -fsSL https://e.intuitum.sh/install.sh | sh

PACKAGE INSTALLERS (available after the first package-enabled release):
 brew install intuitums/tap/e
 npm install -g @intuitums/e
 bun add -g @intuitums/e

UPDATE (use the method you installed with):
 curl or release archive: e update
 npm: npm install -g @intuitums/e@latest
 bun: bun add -g @intuitums/e@latest
 brew: brew update && brew upgrade intuitums/tap/e

VERIFY:
 e --version

START:
 e
 e "why is this function 400 lines long"
 e help

///

SAFETY:
 - Model-directed tools run as your user without a permission prompt by default.
 - Directory trust controls context loading; it does not sandbox execution.
 - Use a container, VM, or OS sandbox when work needs containment.

///

